("t",["Input (x₁, x₂)","(0,0)","(0,1)","(1,0)","(1,1)"],[["Target y","0","1","1","0"],["QNN prediction","0","1","1","0"]],[2.0,1.1,1.1,1.1,1.1]),
("p","XOR is not linearly separable (a single classical perceptron fails). Using ZZFeatureMap (2 features, reps = 1), RealAmplitudes (2 qubits, linear entanglement), squared-error loss and the SPSA optimiser (100 trials), the QNN predicted [0 1 1 0] – **100 % accuracy** on the training data."),
("h","5. Advantages and limitations"),
