("h","3. Worked example – spam detection"),
("b",["Features: x₁ = fraction of capital letters, x₂ = number of links (scaled to [0, π]).","**Angle encoding:** RY(x₁) on q₀, RY(x₂) on q₁, then CNOT to entangle features.","Trainable RY(θ) layers; measure q₀: P(1) > 0.5 ⇒ spam.","After training on labelled e-mails the circuit separates spam from normal mail like a classical classifier, but in a 4-dimensional Hilbert space from only 2 qubits."]),
("h","4. Advantages and challenges"),
